<!-- @before 1. The Threat Model :: guide -->
### Choose the extra trust restriction deliberately

Pinning adds operational restrictions to ordinary certificate and hostname validation; it does not replace them. Define the actual threat, participating networking stacks, installed-client lifetime and recovery path before opting in. Android cautions about the outage risk when server identities change. [Android TLS guidance](https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-ssl) and [Network Security Configuration](https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-config).

<!-- @before 6. The Kill Switch (Pragmatic, Controversial) :: staff -->
### A recovery channel has its own trust boundary

A remotely fetched flag cannot arrive through the very channel that obsolete pins block. An independent recovery mechanism still needs authentication and downgrade resistance. Do not convert a pin mismatch into disabled TLS validation or assume one configuration controls every stack.
